A note on this choice, since it is a decision and not a default:

"All rights reserved" is the most restrictive option, and it is here
because it is the only one that can be relaxed later without consequence.
Publishing under a permissive license is irreversible in practice — once
a copy is out under MIT, that copy stays MIT forever. If this repository
is ever made public and an open license is wanted, replacing this file is
a one-line change; going the other direction is not possible.
